```c
static inline bool ip_mc_may_pull(struct sk_buff *skb, unsigned int len)
{
	if (likely(len <= skb_network_offset(skb) + skb->len))
		return true;
	if (len <= skb->len && !pskb_may_pull(skb, len - skb_network_offset(skb)))
		return true;
	return false;
}
```

Hmm, that's odd — return true on failed pull? Let me actually read it in the source. Also `ipv6_mc_may_pull`. Note: pskb_may_pull is called only when `len <= skb->len` — i.e., total packet bytes exist but not linear. That's precisely the reallocation-relevant case.

So in br_ip4_multicast_igmp3_report:
- Pull #2 at line 928 with `len` including nsrcs*4 — attacker-controlled.
- grec stale use at line 946: `ntohs(grec->grec_nsrcs) == 0`.

